<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Mori clan domain</h1><p class="st-meta">1557 CE – 1600 CE (approx.) · capital Yoshida-Koriyama, later Hiroshima</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The domain of the Mori of Aki, who rose under Mori Motonari to rule most of western Honshu and later led the losing side at Sekigahara.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mori-motonari">Mori Motonari</a>, a minor lord of Aki based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoshida-koriyama-castle">Yoshida-Koriyama</a> castle, built up power between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ouchi-clan">Ouchi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amago-clan">Amago</a>. After defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sue-harukata">Sue Harukata</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-miyajima">Itsukushima</a> in 1555 he destroyed the Ouchi in 1557 and took their lands, and in 1566 he conquered the Amago.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Motonari placed his sons at the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kikkawa-clan">Kikkawa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kobayakawa-clan">Kobayakawa</a> families, the two rivers supporting the Mori, and legend tells of his lesson of three arrows on family unity. The domain covered some ten provinces in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chugoku-region">Chugoku</a> region and had a powerful navy. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mori-terumoto">Terumoto</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a>, then made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> in 1582 and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a> in 1589.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mori-terumoto">Terumoto</a> was nominal commander of the western army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> in 1600. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> reduced Mori lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suo-province">Suo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagato-province">Nagato</a>, which became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/choshu-domain">Choshu Domain</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1557 CE – 1600 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Korea and Japan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:90.69%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1557 CE – 1600 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Yoshida-Koriyama, later Hiroshima</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mori Motonari, Mori Terumoto</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Japanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mori clan, Mori of Aki</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1578&amp;focus=mori-clan-domain" aria-label="Mori clan domain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8152 880 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mori clan domain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8347 1195h0M8440 1178h0M8341 1187h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8472 1136h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M8472 1136h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Japan. <a href="/atlas?year=1578&amp;focus=mori-clan-domain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
